Here in the newsgroup, there's always grumblings about things wrong with
Nethack, so here's some more. I'm curious what others' pet peeves are as
well.

- Instant death without warning. This is something that always gets my goat.
There are a lot of ways in the game that a player can die instantly without
even really knowing what happened. For example, hands up everyone who after
countless hours of playing finally developed a character good enouh to make
it to the Medusa level and was promptly killed by drowining (those damn eels),
and then later killed by gazing on Medusa - "Medusa? What Medusa? What's going
on here?
Another example is the whole drawbridge idea. I remember the first time I
made it to the castle (I remember it so well because it was just a few weeks
ago) - there I was staving off the oncoming hoardes (and doing a pretty good
job of it), when all of a sudden someone zaps a wand of striking at me: "You
are blown apart by the debris -More- Do you want your possessions identifed?"
Grrr...  An even worse case of this is in Lord Surtur's lair (applicible to
Valks only, I know) where there's no suggestion at all that a drawbridge
is even there, yet the death comes just as swiftly.
Nethack seems to have a tradition that each time a player makes it just a
little further, something unexpected will pop up and destroy the unwitting
player, but I'm not so sure this is a good thing. Is it any wonder that a lot
of folks use save backups? An alternative might be to give players a warning.
Right now, mind flayers don't kill you outright, you gradually lose
intelligence first, giving you the idea that "Hey, maybe I'd better put a stop
to this!" When you fall into lava, you're given a few moves to escape. Might
it be better to, for drawbridge, for example, say "The drawbridge lurches under
the force from the wand" or somesuch first to give some warning?

- Does anyone else think that wishes are *way* too easy to come by in the
game? Between (trying to be subtle to avoid spoilers) *that* kind of lamp,
*that* kind of potion, and WoW, they're not all that uncommon, especially if
you're looking for one. (E.g., if I want a wish, I can often get one via the
Gnome Town's lighting store or a general store somewhere). When you add a
wand of Polymorph into the mix, wishes become even *more* common.

- Not to refuel the debate or anything, but wishing for quest artifacts? Oh
come on! What's the point of a Valk going on her quest, for example, if she
can just wish for the Orb of Fate? I know, she still needs the bell of
opening, but if quest artifacts are so easy to get (as they are now), why not
just make them standard things that don't need quests?
On a more practical (and perhaps more important) level:
   PYEC + WoP = an essentially invulnerably character.
(maybe tourists deserve it for getting that far :)
Now that I think about it,
   PYEC + horn of plenty + patience = an essentially invulnerable character
as well (due to wishing).
I don't know much about the other quest items, except for the Orb of Fate
(nice to have, but not nearly as powerful as the PYEC), so I don't know
if the others are quite so dangerous "in the wrong hands" :)

(By the way, before folks look at the above two comments and say I think the
game is just too easy - I've never ascended - only made it a few levels down
into Ghemmon with my best character.)

That's it. I'll probably think of more to gripe about later, but those are
the major things that come to mind right now.

 


